name: capability
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: |
  Auto-registered when 4eb9d8cf declared `Signal: capability` for "Koru's
  JavaScript output now measures at hand-written JavaScript".

  IT SHOULD NOT HAVE BEEN A NEW TYPE. The registry already carries
  `capability-gained`, `new-capability` and `novel-capability`, and this makes a
  fourth name for one idea — the type was invented at the commit rather than
  chosen from the list, which is exactly how a categorical vocabulary stops
  being categorical.

  Left in place rather than deleted because the commit that emitted it is
  pushed and the ticket derefs to it. Consolidate the four when someone next
  touches this registry; `capability-gained` reads best of them.
